    "title": "Thanks you, Casellas | Letters | rutlandherald.com",
    "text": "I am a co-chair of the Lake Bomoseen Friends Up North group. For decades, our group has been responsible, along with the town of Hubbardton, for the mechanical harvesting of nuisance aquatic weeds from the lake area north of Grady Bridge. We write to publicly acknowledge and thank Doug and Maureen Casella, and Casella Construction Inc., for their incredibly generous support of our efforts.\nThis year we were unable to start harvesting invasive weeds until the third week of July, about three weeks later than we should have started. As a result, the weed infiltration was severe, and it quickly became apparent that the equipment we had been using for decades was not adequate to deal with the problem.",
